  "description": "Codex round 11 P1: backslash handling in source patterns must mirror reference (path-to-regexp ∪ minimatch). (a) Trailing `\\` in source is preserved as a literal `\\` in path-to-regexp's regex, so `/u/foo\\` matches paths with literal `\\` end (decoded from `%5C`) but NOT `/u/foo`. (b) Inner `\\X` for non-glob X (like `\\f`) matches both the de-escaped form (`/u/f` via path-to-regexp) AND the raw form (`/u/\\f` via minimatch's segment-level transparency). (c) Trailing `\\` on a glob source like `/v/*\\` requires literal `\\` end via the Pattern's primary regex; the glob_fallback is disabled because minimatch's compiled regex requires a synthetic `/` suffix that `path.posix.resolve` always strips.",
